  "homologous":{collocations:["homologous recombination","homologous chromosome"],examples:[{en:"There are so many important genes on every chromosome that the loss of both members of a homologous pair would be fatal, wouldn’t even get past embryonic development.",zh:"每一条染色体上都包含了数量巨大的重要基因，而同时丢失一对同源染色体将是致命的，生命甚至通不过胚胎发育期。"}],deepExplanation:""},
  "homologous chromosome":{collocations:[],examples:[{en:"An aneuploid state in which a third homologous chromosome is present in addition to the normal autosomal pair is called trisomy.",zh:"除了正常染色体对以外，还存在有第二种同源染色体的非整倍体状态，被称为三体性。"},{en:"Locus (pl. loci) The position of a gene on a chromosome. Alleles of the same gene occupy the equivalent locus on homologous chromosomes.",zh:"基因位点，基因座：基因在染色体上的位置。等位基因位于同源染色体相对应的位点上。"}],deepExplanation:""},
