  "immune":{collocations:["immune system","immune response","acquired immune deficiency syndrome","immune globulin","immune surveillance","immune complex","immune serum","immune body"],examples:[{en:"Once we’ve had the disease, we’re immune for life.",zh:"我们一旦得过这种病，就获得了终身免疫力。"}],deepExplanation:""},
  "immune system":{collocations:[],examples:[{en:"My immune system is not as strong as it ought to be.",zh:"我的免疫力比较差。"}],deepExplanation:""},
  "immunity":{collocations:["cellular immunity","immunity system","humoral immunity","noise immunity","innate immunity","natural immunity","diplomatic immunity","adaptive immunity"],examples:[{en:"To protect you against small pox or diphtheria, you are vaccinated with a small amount of the toxin, and then your body develops immunity against that toxin.",zh:"为了避免你长小脓包或得白喉病，所以会给你的身体接种小量毒素，然后你的身体会针对这些毒素产生免疫力。"},{en:"Very few people will have any immunity to this particular combination, which is what gives the concern that this will be a pandemic rather than just a normal seasonal flu outbreak.",zh:"因为很少有人具备对这种特别的混合病毒的免疫力。 人们因此担心，这将不仅仅是正常的季节性流感疫情，而是一次传染病的大流行。"}],deepExplanation:""},
