  "verbiage":{collocations:[],examples:[{en:"“No matter how he stuffs his readers with verbiage, it never amounts to a core of truth, ” he said.",zh:"“不管他如何用废话喂饱他的读者，那些话都毫无真实可言，”他说。"},{en:"On his first visit to the US, and in his maiden address to the UN general assembly, Gaddafi fully lived up to his reputation for eccentricity, bloody-mindedness and extreme verbiage.",zh:"这是卡扎菲首次访问美国，也是他第一次在联大发表演讲；而他的表现也没有辜负他“性情古怪、诚心找茬、废话连篇”的名声。"}],deepExplanation:""},
  "verbose":{collocations:[],examples:[{en:"For once, his usually verbose wife was content to listen.",zh:"他那个一贯唠叨的老婆难得一次愿意倾听。"},{en:"Legal writing is often unclear and verbose.",zh:"法律文书往往措辞含糊，行文冗长。"}],deepExplanation:""},
